pe":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"degeneracy d.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","type":"topic"}}}